WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.640
It's Friday. Welcome to Tesla Short's time. Daily episode 491 from May 29th, 2026.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.880
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Let's close out the week with today's Tesla

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:18.760
news. The 2026 Model Y became the first vehicle ever to pass the US government's new Advanced

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:26.500
Driver Assistance Safety Tests. The US government named the 2026 Tesla Model Y, the first vehicle

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:33.760
to clear its updated, advanced driver assistance safety tests. The test covers specific scenarios for

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.580
automatic emergency braking, lane keeping, and forward collision warning performance.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.820
This certification gives Tesla a concrete regulatory edge when marketing supervised driver

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.660
assistance features to buyers. The outcome stems from Tesla's data collection across millions

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:56.560
of miles of real-world driving rather than lab simulations along. Watch for whether other

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:01.480
automakers receive similar clearances in the coming months. That regulatory step in the United

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:07.640
States connects to further progress for the same supervised software in Europe. Estonia approved

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:14.200
Tesla's full self-driving supervised software following earlier clearances in the Netherlands and Lithuania.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:20.580
The decision adds another European market where owners can activate the supervised system on public roads.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:27.360
Regulators reviewed Tesla's safety data package before granting access. This expands the geographic

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:34.320
footprint where FSD features can generate real-world miles and feedback. Next data point will be whether

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:40.360
additional EU countries follow the same path this summer. While those approvals open new markets,

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:46.740
Tesla faces a separate policy dispute in Canada. Tesla said it will pursue legal remedies after

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:53.420
Manitoba removed the company from its provincial EV rebate program. The policy change bars Tesla

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:59.740
vehicles from receiving the incentive that other EV makers still qualify for. Company filings indicate

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:06.400
the move affects both retail and fleet purchases in the province. Tesla argues the exclusion violates

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:12.380
fair competition rules under Canadian trade agreements. The next step depends on whether Manitoba

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:18.200
adjusts the program or the case moves to formal proceedings. In another market update, Tesla

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:24.960
expanded its India lineup. Tesla introduced the Model Y premium rear-wheel drive in India, priced at

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:32.220
50.89 lakh rupees. The new trim expands the local lineup as the company increases its EV presence

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:38.100
in the market. The vehicle includes updated features compared with earlier India spec units.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:43.460
Deliveries are expected to begin once regulatory and logistics steps are complete.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:49.160
Observers will track whether this pricing draws measurable order volume in the coming quarter.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:55.700
Efficiency comparisons are also emerging from another manufacturer. Early testing shows the

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:01.080
upcoming Arabian R2 achieving energy consumption figures comparable to the Tesla Model Y.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:07.000
The R2 carries a bigger and heavier body yet reaches similar efficiency through aerodynamic

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:12.960
and powertrain tuning. Rivian plans to launch higher priced versions first on June 9th with the

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:20.380
$45,000 target model arriving later. The result highlights how battery and motor refinements can offset

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:27.520
mass penalties in the compact SUV segment. Production volume and real-world range data will clarify whether

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:34.260
the efficiency edge holds at scale. Labor actions continue in one European country. The Swedish trade

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:40.100
union has reduced the scope of its years-long strike against Tesla. The adjustment lowers the number

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:45.100
of targeted workplaces and actions while the core dispute over collective bargaining continues.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.820
Tesla has maintained operations that affected sites through alternative staffing and logistics.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:57.160
The downsizing signals a tactical shift rather than resolution of the underlying labor disagreement.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:03.380
Further updates will depend on whether negotiations resume or the reduced actions produce measurable

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:10.060
pressure. On the sales front Tesla has reclaimed the lead. Tesla moved back into the number one

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:16.840
position in worldwide battery electric vehicle deliveries. The shift reflects stronger quarterly volume

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:23.640
compared with key competitors in China and Europe. Production at Giga Shanghai and Giga Texas supported

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:29.960
the rebound. Market share gains came primarily from refreshed Model Y and Model 3 variants.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:35.440
The next quarterly report will show whether the lead holds through summer demand patterns.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:42.660
Tesla also secured a new patent on thermal management. Tesla received a patent covering a method to

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:48.680
keep parked EVs cooler without draining the main battery excessively. The system uses targeted

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:53.700
airflow and thermal management components to reduce cabin temperature during hot weather.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:59.280
It addresses a common owner complaint about heat build-up when vehicles sit in direct sun.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:04.680
The approach could improve comfort on return to the car and reduce the energy needed for

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.760
initial air conditioning. Production integration timing remains unclear from the filing.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.980
Fleet scale in Texas remains limited despite hardware progress.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:21.400
Registration data filed with the Texas DMV shows Tesla operates fewer than 50 robo taxis in the state.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:27.200
This cowd falls well short of earlier public statements about scaling to 1,000 vehicles.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:33.200
The smaller fleet limits the volume of unsupervised miles that can be accumulated for regulatory

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:40.040
review. Waymos Texas operations exceed Tesla's by a significant margin according to the same

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:46.460
filings. Future expansion depends on both vehicle production and state level operating permits.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:53.260
Tesla is also testing new hiring methods at one factory. Tesla is testing a hiring process at

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:59.620
Giga Berlin that uses neural assessment games instead of resume reviews. The approach aims to

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:04.880
measure problem solving potential without relying on prior job titles or education credentials.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:11.140
A pilot program is already running with selected candidates. Results will determine whether the method

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:17.340
expands to other sites or hiring tracks. The shift could alter how engineering and operations roles are

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:24.780
if the data shows improved outcomes. Reports also point to closer coordination between Tesla and another

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:31.780
company. Reports indicate Tesla and SpaceX are quietly aligning certain engineering and manufacturing

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:38.220
functions. The overlap centers on shared AI hardware development and supply chain coordination.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:43.880
No formal merger announcement has been made by either company. The integration could accelerate

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:49.820
progress on autonomy and robotics programs that draw from both organization's resources.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:54.860
Confirmation would likely come through joint project disclosures rather than corporate

00:06:54.860 --> 00:07:01.740
filings. Hardware certification for autonomy has advanced in Texas. Tesla completed certification

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:08.960
of its Robotaxi platform to level four autonomy standards for Texas roads. The designation allows

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:14.280
operation without a safety driver in approved zones once regulatory conditions are met.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:20.160
The certification covers the sensor suite and compute hardware currently installed in test vehicles.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:25.420
This step moves the program past supervised only restrictions in that state.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.720
Deployment scale will still require additional state approvals and fleet expansion.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:36.540
One recent FSD update shows the system handling complex highway situations more smoothly.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:42.420
Tesla posted video showing the system predicting and reacting to poor human driving during

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:48.500
highway merges and exits. The capability comes from training on millions of observed merge events

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:54.660
rather than rule based logic. It allows the vehicle to adjust speed or lane position preemptively.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:59.480
This reduces the chance of last second corrections that can feel abrupt to passengers.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:04.640
The update reflects continued iteration on edge case handling and mixed traffic.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.980
Another autonomous vehicle operator is moving toward purpose built hardware.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:14.460
The company introduced a vehicle designed from the ground up for autonomous ride hailing instead

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:20.680
of retrofitting existing models. The new platform incorporates integrated sensors and compute hardware

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:26.780
optimized for the Robotaxi use case. It differs from earlier conversions of production cars.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:33.760
This marks a shift toward dedicated hardware as fleets scale. Observers are watching how the design

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.780
affects maintenance costs and uptime. Tesla also shared a new image of its

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:45.120
Optimus robot. A recent post shows the humanoid robot in a static pose that highlights updated limb

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:50.960
proportions and actuator placement. The image provides a visual checkpoint on hardware refinements

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:57.040
since earlier public demonstrations. It does not include new performance metrics or task demonstrations.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:02.920
The post aligns with ongoing work at the dedicated Giga Texas Optimus production area.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.860
Further updates are expected as assembly cells come online later this year.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:13.380
There is a challenge worth discussing on the Robotaxi side. Registration

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:20.080
filings reveal Tesla's Texas Robotaxi count sits below 50 vehicles while Waymo operates more than

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:27.140
10 times that number in the same state. The gap limits the rate at which Tesla can collect unsupervised

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:33.380
miles needed for broader regulatory approval. Tesla has stated plans for larger fleets,

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:39.000
but current production and permitting constraints have kept numbers low. Closing the difference will

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:44.380
require both hardware output increases and state level operating clearances that have not yet

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:50.300
materialized. Taking a step back from today's headlines, Tesla is testing a different approach to

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:56.280
hiring at Giga Berlin. The decision to pilot neural assessment games for hiring at Giga Berlin

00:09:56.280 --> 00:10:01.200
challenges the assumption that traditional resumes reliably predict performance in advanced

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:06.660
manufacturing and engineering roles. The approach replaces document review with standardized

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:11.420
tasks that measure problem solving speed and pattern recognition under time pressure.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:16.860
Early internal data from the pilot will need to show measurable differences in later job

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:22.820
performance or retention rates before wider adoption. One concrete benchmark will be whether

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:28.320
candidates selected through games demonstrate higher success rates on first year project milestones

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:34.140
compared with prior cohorts hired through conventional screening. If the method proves effective,

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:39.700
Tesla's vertical integration of talent pipelines could shorten the time from hiring to contribution

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:47.080
on programs such as Optimus Actuator calibration or FSD edge case labeling. That shift would matter

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:52.800
most in locations where rapid scaling of specialized teams determines whether production targets for

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:59.500
new hardware are met on schedule. Keep an eye on whether additional EU countries grant FSD supervised

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:12.660
